d a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th District is an even partisan-blanket seat where first-term Republican Tom Barrett faces Democrat William Lawrence in one of the most expensive House races of the cycle. Outside groups have poured millions against both candidates, and both have worked to distance themselves from national party figures, with Vance campaigning for Republicans and Whitmer appearing with Lawrence.\n\nThe evidence tilts Democratic: an October Emerson poll showed Lawrence ahead by eight among likely voters, prediction markets price his chances in the mid-to-high 70s, and most expert raters call the race a Democratic-leaning flip opportunity, though several still rate it a tossup. The race remains competitive, but the weight of polling, money, and ratings favors Lawrence by a modest margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6654, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6515, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6531, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6941, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6328, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6566, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11